diff --git a/features/perturbation-quiescence.feature b/features/perturbation-quiescence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bbe66bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/perturbation-quiescence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+@conformance
+Feature: Perturbation quiescence
+  A green tree carries no standing PERTURBATION token in implementation
+  directories. A live perturbation rides uncommitted with its own watchbill
+  entries, so quiescence reddens only where a standing token is a fault.
+
+  Scenario: No standing PERTURBATION token in implementation
+    When the verification-conformance check runs with perturbation quiescence
+    Then no implementation file contains the literal token "PERTURBATION"
diff --git a/features/watchbill-shape-conformance.feature b/features/watchbill-shape-conformance.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..78af8c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/watchbill-shape-conformance.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+@conformance
+Feature: Watchbill shape conformance
+  The watchbill.json conforms to its required shape when present,
+  and is absent at rest.
+
+  Scenario: Absent watchbill conforms by absence
+    Given no watchbill.json exists at the project root
+    Then the deck is at rest
+
+  Scenario: Present watchbill has valid shape
+    Given a watchbill.json exists at the project root
+    Then every watch entry contains only "scenarios" arrays
+    And every scenario reference uses the "<spec>.feature:<Scenario Name>" form
+    And no watch entry contains prose, metadata, or hidden context
